  "worked_solution": "The period of $y=\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x=\\operatorname{csc}\u2061(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=8$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x=\\operatorname{csc}\u2061(x+2\\cdot 8\\cdot \\pi )=\\operatorname{csc}\u2061(x+16\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x=6,$ then $\\operatorname{csc}\u2061(x+16\\pi )=6.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{csc}\u2061(x+16\\pi )+5 & =\\frac{1}{3}(6)+5 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{3}+5 \\\\  & =2+5 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
